HEIF and AVIF plug-in for Lumen 1.2
===================================

Lets Lumen import, show, adjust and export HEIF photos (.heic, .heif):
what iPhones and many other phones and cameras save; and AVIF photos
(.avif): the same container with AV1 inside. 8, 10 and 12-bit photos,
photos stored in tiles, turned and mirrored photos, and Display P3
colour (converted to sRGB) all work. Image sequences (animated AVIF,
HEIF bursts) aren't read.

It is a small program, LumenHEIF, which Lumen runs in the background for
each HEIF or AVIF photo it needs: for a thumbnail it takes the photo's
own small thumbnail (quick); for the viewer and exports it decodes the
photo. Decoding uses NEON when the processor has it.

It lives in Lumen's Plugins directory (!Lumen.Plugins.HEIF); PackMan
puts it there, or drag the HEIF directory from the zip into Lumen's
Plug-ins > Add plug-in window (it works at once), or it is found the
next time Lumen starts. It is a format plug-in: its Plugin file tells
Lumen which files are HEIF and AVIF photos, so it needs Lumen 0.0.37
or later. They are imported once it is there.

Memory: LumenHEIF needs memory only while it works: about 10 MB for a
thumbnail, and about 100 MB to decode a 12 megapixel photo at full size
(roughly 200 MB at 24 megapixels, 400 MB at 48). Allow at least 256 MB
free, and 512 MB or more for photos from newer phones.

The LumenHEIF User Guide is in Guide (Guide.index/html): open it in your
web browser.

